"CSS Values and Units Module Level 4 (https://drafts.csswg.org/css-values-4/)\nciteturn1278view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://drafts.csswg.org/css-values-4/#absolute-lengths\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 2959\nL0: # CSS Values and Units Module Level 4\nL1: \nL2: cite0†Editor’s Draft†www.w3.org , 20 August 2026\nL3: \nL4: More details about this document\nL5: This version:\nL6:     cite1†https://drafts.csswg.org/css-values-4/ L7: Latest published version:\nL8:     cite2†https://www.w3.org/TR/css-values-4/†www.w3.org L9: Feedback:\nL10:     cite3†CSSWG Issues Repository†github.com L11:     cite4†Inline In Spec L12: Editors:\nL13:     cite5†Tab Atkins†xanthir.com (Google)\nL14:     cite6†Elika J. Etemad / fantasai†fantasai.inkedblade.net (Apple)\nL15: Suggest an Edit for this Spec:\nL16:     cite7†GitHub Editor†github.com L17: Test Suite:\nL18:     cite8†https://wpt.fyi/results/css/css-values/†wpt.fyi L19: cite9†Copyright†www.w3.org © 2026 cite10†World Wide Web Consortium†www.w3.org . W3C (World Wide Web Consortium)^{®} cite11†liability†www.w3.org , cite12†trademark†www.w3.org and cite13†permissive document license†www.w3.org rules apply.\nL20: \nL21: * * *\nL22: ## Abstract\nL23: \nL24: This CSS module describes the common values and units that CSS properties accept and the syntax used for describing them in CSS property definitions.\nL25: \nL26: cite14†CSS†www.w3.org is a language for describing the rendering of structured documents (such as HTML and XML) on screen, on paper, etc.\nL27: ## Status of this document\nL28: \nL29: This is a public copy of the editors’ draft. It is provided for discussion only and may change at any moment. Its publication here does not imply endorsement of its contents by W3C. Don’t cite this document other than as work in progress.\nL30: Please send feedback by cite15†filing issues in GitHub†github.com (preferred), including the spec code “css-values” in the title, like this: “[css-values] …summary of comment…”. All issues and comments are cite16†archived†lists.w3.org . Alternately, feedback can be sent to the (cite17†archived†lists.w3.org ) public mailing list www-style@w3.org.\nL31: \nL32: This document is governed by the cite18†18 August 2025 W3C Process Document†www.w3.org .\nL33: ## Table of Contents\nL34:   1. cite19†1 Introduction L35:     1. cite20†1.1 Module Interactions L36:   2. cite21†2 Value Definition Syntax L37:     1. cite22†2.1 Component Value Types L38:     2. cite23†2.2 Component Value Combinators L39:     3. cite24†2.3 Component Value Multipliers L40:     4. cite25†2.4 Combinator and Multiplier Patterns L41:     5. cite26†2.5 Component Values and White Space L42:     6. cite27†2.6 Functional Notation Definitions L43:     7. cite28†2.7 Property Value Examples L44:     8. cite29†2.8 Non-Terminal Definitions and Grammar Production Blocks L45:   3. cite30†3 Combining Values: Interpolation, Addition, and Accumulation L46:     1. cite31†3.1 Range Checking L47:   4. cite32†4 Textual Data Types L48:     1. cite33†4.1 Pre-defined Keywords L49:       1. cite34†4.1.1 CSS-wide keywords: initial, inherit and unset L50:     2. cite35†4.2 Unprefixed Author-defined Identifiers: the <custom-ident> type L51:     3. cite36†4.3 Prefixed Author-defined Identifiers: the <dashed-ident> type L52:     4. cite37†4.4 Quoted Strings: the <string> type L53:     5. cite38†4.5 Resource Locators: the <url> type L54:       1. cite39†4.5.1 Relative URLs L55:         1. cite40†4.5.1.1 Fragment URLs L56:       2. cite41†4.5.2 Empty URLs L57:       3. cite42†4.5.3 URL Modifiers L58:       4. cite43†4.5.4 URL Processing Model L59:   5. cite44†5 Numeric Data Types L60:     1. cite45†5.1 Range Restrictions and Range Definition Notation L61:     2. cite46†5.2 Integers: the <integer> type L62:       1. cite47†5.2